[\"**\`heartbeat(id, token, { leaseMs })\`** returns \`{ leaseUntil }\`. Throws \`StaleLeaseError\` if the lease is no longer yours.\", \"**\`heartbeat(id, token, { leaseMs })\`** returns \`{ leaseUntil }\`. Throws \`StaleLeaseError\` if the lease is no longer yours. The extension is written to the log, so every process sees it, including whichever one runs the reaper.\"],
[\"**\`complete(id, token, result)\`** records the result. Throws \`StaleLeaseError\` if the lease is no longer yours. RFC 007 changes what this returns.\", \"**\`complete(id, token, result)\`** commits the result and returns a receipt \`{ id, outcome, token, result, completedAt, completionSeq }\`. The commit is the moment the record is durable; it happens before the call returns. \`outcome\` is \`'committed'\` the first time. A repeat with the token that committed, even after a restart or a compaction, returns \`outcome: 'already-committed'\` with the stored \`result\`, \`completedAt\` and \`completionSeq\`, ignores the result passed in, and writes nothing. Any other token throws \`StaleLeaseError\` and changes nothing; a job that has been pruned throws \`UnknownJobError\`. A lease past its deadline can still commit, as long as no reaper, reclaim, reclaim or cancel has acted on it. See [rfc-007](rfc-007-exactly-once-completion.md).\n\n**\`getResult(id)\`** returns \`{ id, status: 'done', result, token, attempts, completedAt, completionSeq }\` for a finished job, \`{ id, status }\` for any other, and \`null\` for a job that never existed or has been pruned. Results are kept for \`retainCompletedMs\`.\n\n**\`completions({ after = 0, limit })\`** returns the retained commits in commit order, \`[{ seq, id, token, result, completedAt }]\`, with \`seq > after\`. Numbers start at 1 and go up by one per commit, across restarts and compactions, including after older entries were pruned. Readers keep their own position. Jobs finished before this was added have no number and are not listed.\n\n**\`reclaimWorker(workerId, { reason })\`** gives up every lease held by a worker known to be dead, at once, and returns \`[{ id, status }]\`. Each job is \`ready\` and runnable straight away (no backoff), with \`reason\` as its \`lastError\`, or \`dead\` if it is out of attempts; the attempt counts. Jobs the worker already committed are not touched. The old token is stale from then on. Only call this for a worker that cannot still be running: a worker id names a process, and \`WorkerPool\` makes its ids unique (\`w<n>.<pool id>\`) so that one pool never reclaims another's.\"],
[\"A worker holding the job loses its lease.\", \"A worker holding the job loses its lease.\"],
[\"\`message\` carries worker events (\`kind\` is one of \`ready\`, \`job-started\`, \`job-completed\`, \`job-failed\`, \`job-fenced\`, \`worker-error\`), \`exit\` fires when a worker exits,\", \"\`message\` carries worker events (\`kind\` is one of \`ready\`, \`job-started\`, \`job-completed\`, \`job-failed\`, \`job-fenced\`, \`worker-error\`), \`exit\` fires when a worker exits (the pool has by then reclaimed that worker's leases and is starting a replacement),\"],
[\"- \`stop()\` stops the workers and waits for them to go.\", \"- \`stop()\` stops the workers and waits for them to go.\n\nA worker that has run a handler keeps trying to record the outcome until it is recorded or the worker learns it was fenced (\`job-fenced\`); it keeps heartbeating meanwhile and takes no other job. A \`worker-error\` message is sent for each failed try. A result that cannot be stored at all (not JSON, over the size limit) fails the attempt.\"],
[\"\`stats()\` returns counts by status, plus \`total\`, \`generation\`, \`logBytes\`, \`tornTailsDropped\` and \`lastCompactionError\`.\", \"\`stats()\` returns counts by status, plus \`total\`, \`generation\`, \`logBytes\`, \`tornTailsDropped\` (cut-off writes this process found and removed) and \`lastCompactionError\`.\"],
[\"\`CorruptLogError\` has an \`offset\`.\", \"\`CorruptLogError\` has an \`offset\`; it means damage to records that may have been acknowledged, and the file is left untouched.\"]
]);
"

